parameters.text:
=Draft a professional service agreement using the details below.

Client name: {{ $json.clientName || "[Client Name]" }}
Client email: {{ $json.clientEmail || "[Client Email]" }}
Service tier: {{ $json.serviceTier || "[Service Tier]" }}
Fee: {{ $json.amount ? $json.amount + " " + String($json.currency || "USD").toUpperCase() : "[Fee]" }} (one-time, payable via the Stripe checkout link)
Agreement date: {{ $json.agreementDate || "[Agreement Date]" }}

Structure: 1) Parties, 2) Scope of Services for this tier, 3) Fees and Payment, 4) Term and Termination, 5) Confidentiality, 6) Limitation of Liability, 7) Governing Law (leave as [Jurisdiction]), 8) Acceptance. Use plain text with numbered section headings and no markdown. Keep it under 450 words. Use bracketed placeholders for anything not provided. Do not invent deliverables, dates, jurisdiction, legal terms or facts beyond what is given.

parameters.jsCode:
const text = String($input.first().json.text || "").trim();
if (!text) {
  throw new Error("Contract Agent: model returned empty text");
}
return [{ json: { text } }];
